Article 4 Where a person who conceals or disguises crime proceeds and income therefrom pleads guilty and accepts punishment and actively cooperates in the recovery of crime proceeds and income therefrom, and falls under any of the following circumstances with minor circumstances, no prosecution may be initiated or exemption from criminal punishment may be granted:
(1) Having statutory circumstances for lenient punishment;
(2) Concealing or disguising crime proceeds and income therefrom for close relatives and being a first-time or occasional offender;
(3) Playing a significant role in assisting judicial authorities in tracing the upstream crime;
(4) Other circumstances where the circumstances are minor and the harm is not significant.

Article 5 Where the upstream crime is a crime with a relatively high conviction and sentencing amount standard, such as the crime of illegal mining, and the amount of concealed or disguised crime proceeds and income therefrom reaches 5,000,000 yuan or more, and falls under any of the following circumstances, it may be determined as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 312 of the Criminal Law:
(1) Committing the act of concealing or disguising multiple times;
(2) Knowingly concealing or disguising crime proceeds and income therefrom that are specific funds or goods such as electric power equipment, transportation facilities, radio and television facilities, public telecommunications facilities, military facilities, or funds for disaster relief, emergency rescue, flood control, special care for entitled groups, resettlement, relief, epidemic prevention, social donations, social insurance funds, etc.;
(3) Refusing to cooperate with the recovery of property, resulting in the inability to recover the stolen money or goods;
(4) Causing losses of 2,500,000 yuan or more;
(5) Other circumstances involving serious circumstances.
Where the upstream crime is a crime other than those provided in the preceding paragraph, and the amount of concealed or disguised crime proceeds and income therefrom reaches 500,000 yuan or more, and falls under any of the circumstances in items (1), (2), (3), or (5) of the preceding paragraph, or causes losses of 250,000 yuan or more, it may be determined as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 312 of the Criminal Law.
When determining "serious circumstances", attention shall be paid to maintaining sentencing balance with the upstream crime.
